{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry","id":969891,"title":"Silver vs Iron: questions about \"Realistic\" melee weaponry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T07:40:43-07:00","id":969891,"title":"Silver vs Iron: questions about \"Realistic\" melee weaponry","content":"i was talking to a friend of mine who does medieval recreation. He wants to join the game and since he is way into realism when it comes to weapons, he was wondering about the klaives and Silver based weaponry. According to him, if you were to hit a weapon made of silver with one made of Iron, the iron one would shatter the silver (since silver is weaker). so that made me think more about the klaives and weaponry of garous, can someone help me out here?<br /> <br /> i know the answer is &quot;its a roleplaying game, youre overthinking it&quot;. but still, im curious to know","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:58:50-07:00","id":969908,"title":"","content":"Klaives are fetish weapons so the bound spirit makes the weapon stronger......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:59:17-07:00","id":969909,"title":"","content":"Well, a fetish is reinforced by the spirit within, so mystical weapons get a pass (silver weapons can be made as tough as steel weapons with Alchemy or Enchantment Numina too). As for mundane weapons, they will not shatter but they may be damaged enough to make them into just a club. I think that the best way to deal with it would be for any edged mundane silver weapon to become a club when their user botches an attack or parry roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:59:48-07:00","id":969910,"title":"","content":"For the most part he is right...BUT in the case of a klaive the war spirit makes the silver as hard as iron last I remembered (mokol\u00e8 fetishes that are gold have the same thing going)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:08:31-07:00","id":969916,"title":"","content":"Man, I hate posting too slow and just being that guy repeating....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:09:27-07:00","id":969917,"title":"","content":"For the record...the mokol\u00e8 breed book has a section for rules with mundane gold weapons in it .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:12:30-07:00","id":969971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=969909#post969909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a fetish is reinforced by the spirit within, so mystical weapons get a pass (silver weapons can be made as tough as steel weapons with Alchemy or Enchantment Numina too). As for mundane weapons, they will not shatter but they may be damaged enough to make them into just a club. I think that the best way to deal with it would be for any edged mundane silver weapon to become a club when their user botches an attack or parry roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had thought there were rules for silver weapons being damaged, but it looks like the recommendation is only for silver-plated items. Remember that &quot;silver weapons&quot; does not denote &quot;pure silver&quot;. Sterling Silver is definitely mystically pure, even if it's only 92.5% pure chemically, but it's up to the GM to determine whether a silver alloy weapon that is pure enough to hurt Garou is also pure enough to deform during a single combat.<br /> <br /> Further, (W20) Maces, Swords, and Spiked Clubs all do Strength+2 Lethal at Difficulty 6. So the silver weapon would have to deform to the point of being as dull as a baseball bat or a staff to lose its damage potential during combat.<br /> <br /> After combat, you could certainly declare the weapon to be useless until it is repaired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:44:28-07:00","id":969991,"title":"","content":"Silver is not nearly as weak as some people suggest. The efficacy of a silver melee weapon would depend on the weapon though. Silver would be terrible for making swords. Swords need to use a relatively strong metal and silver isn't that, in fact even early iron and bronze limited the size and shape of swords in ancient times. Strength isn't the only concern either, silver is extremely heavy. In fact, silver is almost as heavy as lead. If you made a sword of silver, not only would the blade be in danger of breaking or bending, but it would be incredibly heavy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, something like a silver mace or axe would be good. The head can be as large or small as you like, more or less, and can be reduced in size to maintain a reasonable weight. Also, the head can have thick enough silver that it wont be in danger of breaking from normal use. An axe or mace head doesn't have to support the weight of the weapon, the shaft does this. Finally, an axe or mace head benefits from being sharp, but it isn't as important or as fragile as a sword's edge and is unlikely to lose any killing ability in the course of a fight.<br /> <br /> For smaller weapons, a silver knife might be alright, as the short length allows the weapon to be lighter and it's small size means less stress on the blade. Though it might be a good idea to make a silver knife a little bit thicker than you need it to be so it wont bend if you stab it into a bone or something. Sharpness is more important for knives than the above weapon and so it might be a good idea to repair/sharpen the edge of a silver knife after combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:21:26-07:00","id":970060,"title":"","content":"A silver head on a spear would also be a good compromise, especially if the shaft was banded with steel. While the point may deform on a botch to attack, it would probably not deform on a botch for a parry, as you are parrying with the shaft and not the point. A really evil design would be to have the point deliberately detach after it impaled someone (definable possible with modern mechanisms), which would leave the point buried in the target. Against a Garou, they would suffer one additional die of unsolvable aggravated damage per turn, at least until someone could dig it out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:23:22-07:00","id":970103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970060#post970060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A silver head on a spear would also be a good compromise, especially if the shaft was banded with steel. While the point may deform on a botch to attack, it would probably not deform on a botch for a parry, as you are parrying with the shaft and not the point. A really evil design would be to have the point deliberately detach after it impaled someone (definable possible with modern mechanisms), which would leave the point buried in the target. Against a Garou, they would suffer one additional die of unsolvable aggravated damage per turn, at least until someone could dig it out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recommend a barbed tip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:25:28-07:00","id":970106,"title":"","content":"Not a bad idea, though if the mechanism fails to release, you are suddenly attached to an enraged Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:29:13-07:00","id":970109,"title":"","content":"Also on the realism thing:<br /> <br /> Silver isn't going to shatter in this context. Brittle metals (which are &quot;stronger&quot; in the sense of being more rigid like iron) shatter. Silver is going to deform and warp instead because it has greater malleability, which is an entirely different kind of strength because it means silver can be bent back into shape where iron/steel would need to be reforged if broken that significantly.<br /> <br /> Silver is a much better projectile than hand-to-hand weapon for those reasons (as noted above is behaves more similarly to lead... that thing we make bullets out of), though <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> has the right of it with using blunter silver weapons if you're going hand-to-hand and not magically tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:03:29-07:00","id":970131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=969908#post969908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Klaives are fetish weapons so the bound spirit makes the weapon stronger......</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the forging process before the spirit was bound supposedly had some effect toward making the silver as strong as steel (possibly due to klaive hammer fetishes). Whatever the case, we can probably agree that klaives are firmly out of the region of normal silver weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:30:17-07:00","id":970161,"title":"","content":"Silver bullets tend to do horrible things to civilian firearms because silver is much harder than lead (which destroys the rifling). Smoothbore weapons (like shotguns) and military weapons (because they are designed to be able to tolerate steel bullets and more exotic forms of ammunition), are quite capable of tolerating silver ammo (I cannot even imagine the level of damage that the Barett Model 82A1, a .50 caliber sniper rifle, would do to a Garou if it was using a silver round). So, if you are anticipating running into werewolves, use a 12 gauge shotgun with silver slugs, and you may actually survive the experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:27:04-07:00","id":970226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970161#post970161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver bullets tend to do horrible things to civilian firearms because silver is much harder than lead (which destroys the rifling). Smoothbore weapons (like shotguns) and military weapons (because they are designed to be able to tolerate steel bullets and more exotic forms of ammunition), are quite capable of tolerating silver ammo (I cannot even imagine the level of damage that the Barett Model 82A1, a .50 caliber sniper rifle, would do to a Garou if it was using a silver round). So, if you are anticipating running into werewolves, use a 12 gauge shotgun with silver slugs, and you may actually survive the experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine that at larger calibers, you might run into problems with silver rounds not staying together when the propellant explodes behind it. Gold might, but it's also denser than lead, so it's going to have a sharply truncated range. You can use sabots to alleviate some problems, but if you use a smaller caliber, you'd have less damage and more penetration, which would do less damage to Garou and Fera vulnerable to the metals.<br /> <br /> (Also the Barrett would do about 12 dice damage base. It's not like it's a tank cannon or Mk. 81 bomb.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:30:54-07:00","id":970232,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a silver tipped harpoon would be really nasty for a Garou to get stabbed with. I'm not sure if that is the weapon I would necessarily want, because there might be another werewolf nearby that you couldn't attack because your harpoon is stuck in the first. Silver arrowheads or javelin heads wouldn't be bad.<br /> <br /> In some ways silver makes for good bullets, since it is so dense. There are problems with them though related to the hardness of silver in relation to lead. It is also harder to make silver bullets than lead ones, but that can be overcome with skill and/or resources. Silver shotgun slugs or pellets would be the easiest way to solve the problem. Another solution would be to use sabots, which would allow you to shoot silver bullets out of a variety of rifles, including a .50 BMG.<br /> <br /> As Heavy Arms mentions, bending would probably be a major issue if you unwisely decided to use a silver sword. Instead of becoming a club, the sword would still maintain a dangerous sharp edge, but would very cumbersome to wield because it would be bent off to one direction. You could possibly correct this by stepping on the blade, assuming you had a bit of time to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:14:50-07:00","id":970266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970232#post970232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a silver tipped harpoon would be really nasty for a Garou to get stabbed with. I'm not sure if that is the weapon I would necessarily want, because there might be another werewolf nearby that you couldn't attack because your harpoon is stuck in the first. Silver arrowheads or javelin heads wouldn't be bad.<br /> <br /> In some ways silver makes for good bullets, since it is so dense.<br /> <br /> There are problems with them though related to the hardness of silver in relation to lead. It is also harder to make silver bullets than lead ones, but that can be overcome with skill and/or resources. Silver shotgun slugs or pellets would be the easiest way to solve the problem. Another solution would be to use sabots, which would allow you to shoot silver bullets out of a variety of rifles, including a .50 BMG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though, the round in the sabot is going to be smaller than the actual caliber. It would tear through sooner due to the higher power/cross sectional area ratio and end up doing less damage by exposure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As Heavy Arms mentions, bending would probably be a major issue if you unwisely decided to use a silver sword. Instead of becoming a club, the sword would still maintain a dangerous sharp edge, but would very cumbersome to wield because it would be bent off to one direction. You could possibly correct this by stepping on the blade, assuming you had a bit of time to do it. </div> </div> </div>NB: You probably never have time to do this in a fight against supernaturally fast werewolves who can often disappear and reappear without your knowledge..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:39:50-07:00","id":970278,"title":"","content":"If you are making customized silver ammo you can machine shop up a customized gun for handling it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Klaive thing, there's litterally a skill just for making Klaives, it requires as much understanding to make a single klaive as all other forms of blacksmithing. A silversmithed up &quot;knife&quot; even wtih a spirit bound in it is still not a klaive. This is why they are so special and should be treated as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:48:49-07:00","id":970284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970226#post970226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Also the Barrett would do about 12 dice damage base. It's not like it's a tank cannon or Mk. 81 bomb.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Even a base damage of 12 dice would be sufficient to kill a Garou with two net successes (if not, you have a crippled Garou who can be shot a second time). A squad of ten snipers, five shooters and five spotters, could kill a five person team of Garou in one turn. Which is why the Garou try to maintain the Veil. The Garou are the best melee fighters in cWoD, but they are still vulnerable to ambushes by people using military grade weapons from a distance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:57:33-07:00","id":970288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970284#post970284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even a base damage of 12 dice would be sufficient to kill a Garou with two net successes (if not, you have a crippled Garou who can be shot a second time). A squad of ten snipers, five shooters and five spotters, could kill a five person team of Garou in one turn. Which is why the Garou try to maintain the Veil. The Garou are the best melee fighters in cWoD, but they are still vulnerable to ambushes by people using military grade weapons from a distance.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, that would only give you a coin flip. Also, Primal-Urge exists in the capacity of a danger sense, so the ambush tactic isn't a sure thing, either..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:12:28-07:00","id":970292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970266#post970266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, though, the round in the sabot is going to be smaller than the actual caliber. It would tear through sooner due to the higher power/cross sectional area ratio and end up doing less damage by exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, silver is way harder than lead, which means that it is already more likely to over penetrate. Making the bullet smaller exacerbates that problem. Of course, for a .50 BMG, it would be going so fast that it would probably create a pretty terrible wound channel. It might be appropriate to reduce the damage a bit. Though a .50 silver sabot would likely ignore pretty much any non-magical armor that a humanoid creature could wear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970266#post970266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NB: You probably never have time to do this in a fight against supernaturally fast werewolves who can often disappear and reappear without your knowledge..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, bending your silver sword back into shape may only take a few seconds, but that can be an eternity in a fight for your life - even against a normal human. Though, as has been discussed, a silver sword is a bad idea anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:43:38-07:00","id":970307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970292#post970292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, silver is way harder than lead, which means that it is already more likely to over penetrate. Making the bullet smaller exacerbates that problem. Of course, for a .50 BMG, it would be going so fast that it would probably create a pretty terrible wound channel. It might be appropriate to reduce the damage a bit. Though a .50 silver sabot would likely ignore pretty much any non-magical armor that a humanoid creature could wear.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are supernaturally resilient and significantly more mass than a human being so over penetration may not be an issue. One might even argue that they might take MORE damage because they can put up more resillience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:53:23-07:00","id":970309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970307#post970307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves are supernaturally resilient and significantly more mass than a human being so over penetration may not be an issue. One might even argue that they might take MORE damage because they can put up more resillience.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's definitely going to be an issue, because there's a lot of space it can whizz through and still not hit vital organs as such. The wound channel will also be significantly less than a normal BMG round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:29:49-07:00","id":970331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970309#post970309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's definitely going to be an issue, because there's a lot of space it can whizz through and still not hit vital organs as such. The wound channel will also be significantly less than a normal BMG round.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> a garou in crinos is functionally walking around with meat that is as resilient as the best armor plating we have. Thus a round should mroe likely be treated as if someone were shot through armor rather than simple meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:06:05-07:00","id":970356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970331#post970331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> a garou in crinos is functionally walking around with meat that is as resilient as the best armor plating we have. Thus a round should mroe likely be treated as if someone were shot through armor rather than simple meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if it's silver. Garou in crinos and just as resilient as humans are (not so much) vs bullets made of silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:07:39-07:00","id":970358,"title":"","content":"Yeah Lian, I'm with SOS on this one. Werewolves are more resilient than humans but they don't have the density of steel. A .50 BMG round is going to go right through the engine block of a truck like a hot knife through butter. It will totally overpenetrate a Garou. <br /> <br /> That problem can be solved by using a .12 gauge rifled shotgun with slug rounds. Much lower muzzle velocity with much greater cross-sectional resistance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:57:20-07:00","id":970384,"title":"","content":"Overpenetration is a meaningless abstraction when the round leaves a sizzling hole the size of a human head in the target (one that the Garou cannot regenerate under normal circumstances). Even if the Garou survives the first shot, they are probably not going to survive the second one. With a maximum effective range of over 1,800 meters, a Garou will also be unlikely to get close enough to you to do any harm before you kill it (and that is why your spotter is equipped with a shotgun with silver slugs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:06:21-07:00","id":970394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970384#post970384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overpenetration is a meaningless abstraction when the round leaves a sizzling hole the size of a human head in the target (one that the Garou cannot regenerate under normal circumstances). Even if the Garou survives the first shot, they are probably not going to survive the second one. With a maximum effective range of over 1,800 meters, a Garou will also be unlikely to get close enough to you to do any harm before you kill it (and that is why your spotter is equipped with a shotgun with silver slugs).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably true. When a bullet has the massive energy that a .50 BMG sabot is going to have, it might not matter that much. Silver essentially treats a werewolf as though it is a mundane being when it comes to damage and I don't imagine any similarly sized creature (like a grizzly bear) is going to be feeling very well after getting hit by a .50 bullet. Though maybe 12 dice of damage is too low for a .50 rifle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:11:24-07:00","id":970397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970384#post970384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overpenetration is a meaningless abstraction when the round leaves a sizzling hole the size of a human head in the target (one that the Garou cannot regenerate under normal circumstances). Even if the Garou survives the first shot, they are probably not going to survive the second one. With a maximum effective range of over 1,800 meters, a Garou will also be unlikely to get close enough to you to do any harm before you kill it (and that is why your spotter is equipped with a shotgun with silver slugs).</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Garou gets hurt with a shot like that and survives you won't get a second shot (generally) because they will disappear. Only the dumbest cubs would stick around, and they would deserve their fate.<br /> Also, on the maximum range, it's hard to take Garou by surprise in the wilderness where they typically are.<br /> So in any case, yes, high powered rifles with silver can kill Garou. But the same could be said of most Supernaturals in the WoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:23:06-07:00","id":970443,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, from a sufficiently long distance, you can hear the report of a bullet before it hits and can dodge. With super senses and speed, I'd expect that Garou would be able to as well, even many cubs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970394#post970394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is probably true. When a bullet has the massive energy that a .50 BMG sabot is going to have, it might not matter that much. Silver essentially treats a werewolf as though it is a mundane being when it comes to damage and I don't imagine any similarly sized creature (like a grizzly bear) is going to be feeling very well after getting hit by a .50 bullet. Though maybe 12 dice of damage is too low for a .50 rifle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree. You run into a lot of problems with random damage, but at some point, you have to stop adding dice, because any more and you'll start bumping into where 30mm cannons should be and then where tank guns should be, and a Barrett might do a lot of damage, but it has to stop somewhere well short of being a danger to modern tanks. There's a reason that high-caliber rifles stopped being called anti-tank rifles, and it's because even the 25mm versions aren't really a threat to modern tank armor, or even in the neighborhood of being a threat. You'd need a 100+mm projectile for that, typically fired from the main gun of another tank.<br /> <br /> 12 dice is already beefed up from where the V2nd edition player's guide put BMG machine guns (8 dice). Any more and you'll be getting into light artillery, which by itself might need a redo, but it's an indicator that you should rethink trying to paint anti-materiel rifles as universal totems of instant death. Try the cannons on the Yamato or the new railgun systems instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:49:09-07:00","id":970453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970443#post970443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, from a sufficiently long distance, you can hear the report of a bullet before it hits and can dodge. With super senses and speed, I'd expect that Garou would be able to as well, even many cubs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtually all rifle bullets go faster than the speed of sound and so no, you can't hear them before they hit. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970443#post970443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would disagree. You run into a lot of problems with random damage, but at some point, you have to stop adding dice, because any more and you'll start bumping into where 30mm cannons should be and then where tank guns should be, and a Barrett might do a lot of damage, but it has to stop somewhere well short of being a danger to modern tanks. There's a reason that high-caliber rifles stopped being called anti-tank rifles, and it's because even the 25mm versions aren't really a threat to modern tank armor, or even in the neighborhood of being a threat. You'd need a 100+mm projectile for that, typically fired from the main gun of another tank.<br /> <br /> 12 dice is already beefed up from where the V2nd edition player's guide put BMG machine guns (8 dice). Any more and you'll be getting into light artillery, which by itself might need a redo, but it's an indicator that you should rethink trying to paint anti-materiel rifles as universal totems of instant death. Try the cannons on the Yamato or the new railgun systems instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>WW, like many RPG's, doesn't scale up that well. It is possible for a human to survive a .50 BMG shot if it hits some extremity, but if a sniper hits the body or head of someone with a .50 then that person is almost certainly going to die. Of course, supernatural protection or resistance can mitigate this, but silver overcomes a werewolf's supernatural resistance to damage and regeneration, so I think that it should be pretty rare for a werewolf to survive a .50 body or head shot with silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:53:21-07:00","id":970455,"title":"","content":"While I can see the argument that &quot;SIlver just negates their supernatural powers&quot; I'm going to counter point silver intrinsically hurts garou outside breed form. Rather than turning off their powers I would say the unsoakability is rather from silver being so damaging to them. However the mechanics are pretty grainy so it could be either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:56:57-07:00","id":970457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970453#post970453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> WW, like many RPG's, doesn't scale up that well. It is possible for a human to survive a .50 BMG shot if it hits some extremity, but if a sniper hits the body or head of someone with a .50 then that person is almost certainly going to die. Of course, supernatural protection or resistance can mitigate this, but silver overcomes a werewolf's supernatural resistance to damage and regeneration, so I think that it should be pretty rare for a werewolf to survive a .50 body or head shot with silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>And by the system it is. 12 dice of damage plus additional damage from successes to hit (assume 2 added damage?) should give you an average of 7 damage which is enough to kill.<br /> <br /> Supernatural regeneration (Rage roll to recover) though, as always, will allow the Garou <i>a chance</i> to survive. Added damage (higher base rifle damage) though wouldn't really affect that part of the equation either way. Rolling low on damage though would specifically indicate a grazing shot (hence why it didn't kill).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:01:36-07:00","id":970461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970453#post970453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Virtually all rifle bullets go faster than the speed of sound and so no, you can't hear them before they hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, at sniping ranges of sufficient length, you can, particularly if you also see the muzzle flash or the light reflecting off the scope. It's a known factor for sniping from particularly long distances; the bullet's travel is far from instantaneous at what would be a true &quot;safe from Garou&quot; range, and a jacked-up superhuman being could probably manage this feat far more often than normal mortal beings of only flesh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WW, like many RPG's, doesn't scale up that well. It is possible for a human to survive a .50 BMG shot if it hits some extremity, but if a sniper hits the body or head of someone with a .50 then that person is almost certainly going to die. Of course, supernatural protection or resistance can mitigate this, but silver overcomes a werewolf's supernatural resistance to damage and regeneration, so I think that it should be pretty rare for a werewolf to survive a .50 body or head shot with silver. </div> </div> </div>Much of the supernatural resistance to damage and healing, but it still heals way faster than injuries of the same magnitude on a human, since in one week, everything has healed up. Also, we're talking about a sup-penetrator in a sabot, which is going to necessarily be of a smaller caliber. Finally, high-Rage Garou can survive due to anger-based recovery, albeit with some nasty scars to show for it.<br /> <br /> This scenario is still very much context-free as to how it goes down and how it got set up. Never change, white room snipers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:07:28-07:00","id":970466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970461#post970461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This scenario is still very much context-free as to how it goes down and how it got set up. Never change, white room snipers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha. Gotta love how this comes up. Every. Single. Time.<br /> <br /> ...and almost always against Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:46:10-07:00","id":970534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970384#post970384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overpenetration is a meaningless abstraction when the round leaves a sizzling hole the size of a human head in the target ...</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, to be fair, the whole White Wolf combat system is a meaningless abstraction.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about &quot;realism&quot; (the supposed target of this whole thread), overpenetration is indeed an issue. The only really important issue with regard to ballistic projectiles is energy deposit. If you have a projectile that massively overpenetrates the target, that's a whole butt-load of kinetic energy that gets deposited somewhere <i>other</i> than the target (this is one of the reasons that you don't generally see battle rifles in service anymore). In practical terms, once you get up to about .30 caliber in small arms, against man-sized targets, you begin encountering the phenomenon of decreasing returns for any comparable increase in bore diameter. Since combat in WoD uses a generally &quot;meaningless abstraction&quot;, this little issue is simply ignored.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:57:40-07:00","id":970625,"title":"","content":"I am not sure of the preferability of small caliber rounds on the battlefield. The capability of larger caliber rounds to effectively penetrate ballistic panels and hard cover is an asset, as is the extraordinary effective ranges of large caliber rounds for sniping purposes. If we ever face an equal army again (as opposed to guerrilla fighters or archaic forces that offer no more challenge than target practice), we may regret our preference for lighter rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:20:26-07:00","id":971002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=970625#post970625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure of the preferability of small caliber rounds on the battlefield. The capability of larger caliber rounds to effectively penetrate ballistic panels and hard cover is an asset, as is the extraordinary effective ranges of large caliber rounds for sniping purposes. If we ever face an equal army again (as opposed to guerrilla fighters or archaic forces that offer no more challenge than target practice), we may regret our preference for lighter rounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere's actually some discussion about that very subject in several quarters. The venerable M-14 battle rifle has actually made a modest comeback with designated marksmen (though because of its range, rather than its lethality), and I have it on good authority that various people in the special forces community are favoring the 7.62mm weapons for that <i>and</i> lethality reasons. The likelihood of encountering body-armor is another factor in the arguments for shifting away from the 5.56mm round. Nonetheless, TRADOC did a whole butt-load of assessments that showed that the assault rifle is still a better concept than the battle rifle because of volume of fire issues. Now, personally I'm not a huge fan of the M-16 or that entire family and would <i>much</i> prefer to have a .30 caliber weapon in my hands if they ever send my sorry butt downrange, but I'm a support weenie so my opinion doesn't count for much. I<i> seriously </i>doubt that the dinky little .22 crap is going away anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:35:44-07:00","id":971017,"title":"","content":"The US army is the least accurate army in world history. The US army fired 250,000 bullets for every enemy combatant killed in Afghanistan and Iraq, which is twenty percent of the kill ratio that the US army had in Vietnam and four percent of the kill ratio that the US army had in World War Two. Either people in the Afghanistan and Iraq are twenty-five times harder to kill than the Germans and the Japanese were in World War Two or else we are using the wrong weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:24:33-07:00","id":971052,"title":"","content":"That figure is always a bit misleading. One of the reasons the bullets fired per kill has gone up, is because it includes training and practice ammunition use, and the US military has increased required range times. As well, there's a change in technology, going along with changes in tactics, and changes in enemy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though we're drifting pretty far off topic at this point. WtA doesn't really deal with large scale human military stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T18:49:26-07:00","id":971066,"title":"","content":"Ahem, also the mere fact that the assault rifle has supplanted the battle rifle, and the doctrine has changed contributes. Squad support weapons are also now much more common than in world war II, and the M-249 and M-240 have supplanted the BAR, which had a relatively small box magazine. Those two weapons use belted ammunition. In short, the ammunition use is much more profligate and most of it is not aimed. Accuracy of aimed shots has probably not declined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:08:10-07:00","id":971130,"title":"","content":"I am not quite sure if there are many aimed shots anymore (outside of special forces and snipers). Most of the Marines that I knew who served in Iraq were more 'spray and pray' during any encounter, which probably explained most of the civilian casualties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T23:28:46-07:00","id":971180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=971130#post971130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not quite sure if there are many aimed shots anymore (outside of special forces and snipers). Most of the Marines that I knew who served in Iraq were more 'spray and pray' during any encounter, which probably explained most of the civilian casualties.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThe fact that we're up against adversaries who actively hide among and masquerade as civilians is what explains the civilian casualties. That's why the Geneva Convention (and much of the Customary Law of Land Warfare) is so focused on the requirements for uniforms and &quot;distinctive signs&quot;. If you can't tell the wolves from the sheep, you will start to assume all the sheep have fangs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T01:09:48-07:00","id":971197,"title":"","content":"As well, with the proliferation of lighter weight, and high ammo count automatic weapons, high levels of suppressing fire is a more common tactic. It's not &quot;spray and pray.&quot; It's, &quot;spray to keep them down while the rest of the fire team/squad maneuvers for cleaner shots.&quot; Which is an ammunition heavy tactic that's relatively effective otherwise made possible by the weapons <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3506_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3506\" data-vbnamecard=\"3506\">Uniform Two Six</a> just mentioned.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> To try to bring this back around to the thread topic, that's actually one of the issues with silver that we haven't really discussed. Besides the insane expense of 100+ silver bullets, one of the issues that would face any attempt to use current military automatic weapons is going to be weight. Ammunition gets heavy (and silver isn't exactly going to help) - which is incidentally one of the reason to favor the smaller caliber assault rifles as standard issue - and trying to lug around enough ammo for either a lot of shooting, or the tactics that are ammo intensive is going to be an issue if unit maneuverability on foot is going to be a significant tactical factor.<br /> <br /> So this returns to focusing on things like a shotgun for silver slugs rather than getting into the issue of higher volume capable weapons and silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T07:12:56-07:00","id":971309,"title":"","content":"Silver has slightly less density than lead, so the ammunition weight would not be an issue in most cases. I do agree that silver slugs make the most sense overall though, but you have to have the skill to make your own ammo. The Gunsmithing secondary ability would be a good investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:29:53-07:00","id":971332,"title":"","content":"Shotguns would certainly be easier to make bullets for from a technical standpoint. I guess you could even use links from a silver chain for silver shot. A shotgun doesn't give you the advantage of sniping, but if you're fighting relatively close it's going to be good. Silver isn't so expensive that silver weapons are reserved for the wealthy, but if you're on a budget then you probably do want to avoid things like suppressive fire with silver bullets. <br /> <br /> Though I can just imagine a cash strapped werewolf hunter getting out his knife to dig out silver bullets from bodies, the ground, trees, or wherever else they may have become lodged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:33:09-07:00","id":971333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=971309#post971309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gunsmithing secondary ability would be a good investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been the case for Werewolf hunters. It draws a lot less attention too when you don't have to go around shopping for someone willing to make you silver bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:45:42-07:00","id":971336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=971333#post971333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has always been the case for Werewolf hunters. It draws a lot less attention too when you don't have to go around shopping for someone willing to make you silver bullets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that would certainly come in handy. Though I would be willing to guess that Pentex/Herculean Forearms probably has a factory set up somewhere that specializes in making silver bullets and they would have the resources and technical ability to overcome possible downsides of silver bullets. They might even provide these bullets for sale, supposedly as collectors items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:09:23-07:00","id":971346,"title":"","content":"I think that silver bullets would be more 'specialty' items sold to the more lunatic fringe of gun dealers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:34:29-07:00","id":971753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/969891-silver-vs-iron-questions-about-realistic-melee-weaponry?p=971332#post971332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shotguns would certainly be easier to make bullets for from a technical standpoint. I guess you could even use links from a silver chain for silver shot. A shotgun doesn't give you the advantage of sniping, but if you're fighting relatively close it's going to be good. Silver isn't so expensive that silver weapons are reserved for the wealthy, but if you're on a budget then you probably do want to avoid things like suppressive fire with silver bullets.<br /> <br /> Though I can just imagine a cash strapped werewolf hunter getting out his knife to dig out silver bullets from bodies, the ground, trees, or wherever else they may have become lodged.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Werewolf hunting is a richman's sport. Poor people hunt vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}